{"name":"Deep Space Royal","hex":"#223382","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"space","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Unlimited or generalized extent, physical or otherwise.\nThe distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The distance between objects. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To roam, walk, wander.","To set some distance apart."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/space"},{"term":"royal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a monarch or his (or her) family.","Having the air or demeanour of a monarch; illustrious; magnanimous; of more than common size or excellence."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A royal person; a member of a royal family.","A standard size of printing paper, measuring 25 by 20 inches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Space","blocks":[{"text":"Space is a three-dimensional continuum containing positions and directions. In classical physics, physical space is often conceived in three linear dimensions. Modern physicists usually consider it, with time, to be part of a boundless four-dimensional continuum known as spacetime. The concept of space is considered to be of fundamental importance to an understanding of the physical universe. However, disagreement continues between philosophers over wh